# the Bar page writes steps as Steps does: a kit's white keys toggle steps (on the bar OCT picks), a black key picks
# the sound, a held step takes black keys as its sounds and ARP its tricks; a synth track's black keys stay the scale,
# its white keys write the notes played last, a held step's second white key its length
wait 300
expect trk 1
tap SEQ
turn SELECT 1
expect page Bar
tapkey w0
expect note 1 1 1 1
tapkey b1
tapkey w4
expect note 1 1 5 2
tap OCT+
tapkey w0
expect note 1 1 17 2
tap OCT-
key w2 down
wait 60
tapkey b2
key w2 up
expect note 1 1 3 3
key w4 down
wait 60
tap ARP
turn K1 3
turn K2 1
wait 40
shot bar_trick.png
key w4 up
expect comp 1 5 3
expect note 1 1 5 2
wait 40
shot bar_kit.png
spin ALGO 2
expect trk 3
tapkey 0
tap SEQ
turn SELECT 1
expect page Bar
tapkey w1
expect note 3 1 2 60
key w4 down
wait 60
tapkey w6
key w4 up
tapkey b1
expect page Bar
wait 40
shot bar_synth.png
